      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-60038",
      ":question/problem": "Paul has a car that can travel $80$ miles with $3$ gallons of gas. He creates a ratio table to determine the ratio of miles to gallons for different quantities.\n\n| Miles | Gallons |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $80$ | $3$ |\n| $160$ | $6$ |\n| $$? | $12$ |\n\nHow many miles can he travel with $12$ gallons of gas?"
